WEBVTT

00:06.400 --> 00:13.530
<b>The Apothecary Diaries</b>

00:06.400 --> 00:13.530
<b>The Apothecary Diaries</b>

01:30.990 --> 01:33.990
This story is a work of fiction. The names of all of the characters, organizations, and so on
 are imaginary. It also bears no connection to any specific real-life events.

01:51.570 --> 01:53.470
We have eagerly awaited your arrival.

02:06.480 --> 02:10.480
Episode 52: The Last Volume

02:08.980 --> 02:10.940
Have you finished changing?

02:11.240 --> 02:12.140
Yes.

02:15.160 --> 02:16.200
Please, this way.

02:21.510 --> 02:23.590
<i>Impressive. This was 
the emperor's villa after all.</i>

02:23.590 --> 02:27.800
<i>Now it's the home of a former 
member of the Four Ladies.</i>

02:29.910 --> 02:31.280
She is here.

02:32.610 --> 02:33.630
Welcome.

02:33.960 --> 02:36.180
It's been a long time, Lady Ah-Duo.

02:36.710 --> 02:39.170
So, you have business with her today?

02:39.170 --> 02:39.890
Yes.

02:40.350 --> 02:44.780
<i>Suirei is the late emperor's grandchild, 
but is also related to the Shi clan.</i>

02:45.570 --> 02:48.260
<i>She can't step out into public anymore.</i>

02:48.260 --> 02:51.320
<i>She will most likely live out 
the rest of her life in captivity.</i>

02:51.900 --> 02:54.070
<i>What does she plan to do from now on?</i>

02:54.070 --> 02:56.270
<i>What is the emperor going to do with her?</i>

02:56.270 --> 02:59.760
<i>I have no idea, but given how skilled 
she is as an apothecary,</i>

02:59.760 --> 03:02.550
<i>it would be a waste for her 
to stay hidden like this.</i>

03:02.550 --> 03:06.500
I will stay here, but don't mind me, 
talk amongst yourselves.

03:06.500 --> 03:08.190
I understand. Thank you.

03:12.400 --> 03:15.940
<i>I can't help but mind her, but...</i>

03:19.520 --> 03:21.880
Do you remember these?

03:24.700 --> 03:26.850
They were used by my master.

03:27.310 --> 03:28.730
Is this the whole series?

03:29.380 --> 03:30.860
It's missing one.

03:31.220 --> 03:34.110
I believe there were fifteen books.

03:34.620 --> 03:37.490
Do you have any idea where
 the last remaining volume is?

03:38.860 --> 03:39.990
No, I don't.

03:40.520 --> 03:42.740
<i>She doesn't seem to be lying.</i>

03:42.740 --> 03:45.380
<i>She's got no reason to, regardless.</i>

03:45.380 --> 03:49.430
So, this "master" of yours, 
where is he now?

03:51.260 --> 03:53.250
He is alive, isn't he?

03:55.510 --> 03:58.260
The resurrection potion that you used...

03:58.260 --> 04:01.730
He tested it on himself, didn't he?

04:03.550 --> 04:05.060
That's correct.

04:05.430 --> 04:09.720
If he didn't, there was no way he 
could have escaped that stronghold.

04:10.310 --> 04:14.940
But he probably wouldn't be able 
to answer your questions.

04:15.260 --> 04:17.040
What do you mean?

04:17.040 --> 04:21.070
Kyou-u... I mean, his new 
name is Chou-u, I guess.

04:21.510 --> 04:25.920
He lost his memories 
and is paralyzed on one side.

04:25.920 --> 04:27.920
Does that give you any hints?

04:27.920 --> 04:30.580
You're saying he lost his memories?

04:31.100 --> 04:34.000
It's a little different, but similar.

04:34.590 --> 04:38.240
In fact, you may have passed by him 
without noticing.

04:38.640 --> 04:40.510
What do you mean?

04:41.170 --> 04:43.390
Do you remember the hot spring resort?

04:44.180 --> 04:45.260
Yes.

04:45.780 --> 04:48.960
The hidden village, worshipping the fox.

04:49.640 --> 04:53.900
My master is one of 
the bedridden old men there.

04:54.980 --> 04:57.780
<i>That place was being used 
as a hot spring sanatorium.</i>

04:58.080 --> 05:02.720
<i>She snuck him in there as one of 
the sick, to hide him from Shenmei.</i>

05:03.360 --> 05:07.200
He doesn't remember who he is anymore.

05:07.200 --> 05:08.870
If he'd been in good shape,

05:10.140 --> 05:15.400
<i>she</i> wouldn't have thought of getting 
you involved in the incident.

05:16.210 --> 05:18.210
<i>Suirei must have noticed.</i>

05:19.010 --> 05:21.030
<i>Shisui did all of that 
to work with her father</i>

05:21.030 --> 05:24.350
<i>to reveal all the evil 
hidden in this nation.</i>

05:24.640 --> 05:28.600
<i>And to release her sister from her mother.</i>

05:29.520 --> 05:32.150
<i>If Suirei's master was available,</i>

05:32.150 --> 05:36.270
<i>they wouldn't have had to 
take me to that stronghold.</i>

05:37.110 --> 05:39.610
<i>No clues, I guess.</i>

05:39.610 --> 05:42.740
<i>I thought I finally had something.</i>

05:43.130 --> 05:48.080
In that case, do you know anything 
about the locusts he was studying?

05:48.870 --> 05:51.860
I wasn't part of that research.

05:51.860 --> 05:53.620
I'm not good with insects...

05:53.620 --> 05:57.040
That was <i>her</i> area of expertise.

05:58.630 --> 06:00.170
I understand.

06:00.590 --> 06:03.720
<i>And "she" is no longer with us.</i>

06:05.540 --> 06:08.390
When we were ordered to 
create the immortality potion,

06:08.690 --> 06:12.420
they destroyed most of 
the research material.

06:12.420 --> 06:15.400
The contents of that room is 
pretty much all that remains.

06:15.820 --> 06:18.850
<i>But the master, 
wanting to continue his studies,</i>

06:18.850 --> 06:24.900
<i>used his guard Sazen
to do research. I see.</i>

06:25.320 --> 06:29.120
This girl you keep talking about, 
she must have been very smart.

06:30.010 --> 06:33.330
No matter how smart... 
She's no longer with us.

06:37.640 --> 06:42.210
So, if she's so smart, would she go 
without leaving anything behind?

06:47.670 --> 06:49.580
I-I'm sorry.

06:49.580 --> 06:51.930
Don't worry. Relax.

06:51.930 --> 06:53.940
I don't like formalities, anyway.

06:54.520 --> 06:59.190
Look at her. She's lost in thought, with 
manners and whatnot out the window.

06:59.520 --> 07:03.070
<i>No, I understand I was 
supposed to apologize there.</i>

07:03.500 --> 07:07.750
<i>If Shisui left something behind...
 Where would it be?</i>

07:11.870 --> 07:12.660
<i>The stronghold?</i>

07:13.700 --> 07:14.540
<i>The rear palace?</i>

07:15.730 --> 07:16.670
<i>The medical office?</i>

07:18.030 --> 07:19.340
<i>No.</i>

07:20.990 --> 07:22.170
<i>That's...</i>

07:28.200 --> 07:29.470
<i>The clinic...</i>

07:29.700 --> 07:30.930
The clinic!

07:32.640 --> 07:34.900
<i>Right before getting abducted 
from the rear palace,</i>

07:34.900 --> 07:37.600
<i>I did see the book of insects there.</i>

07:37.600 --> 07:40.110
<i>Oh, Shisui, you're...</i>

07:43.760 --> 07:45.740
<i>So cunning!</i>

07:49.090 --> 07:50.240
This is it, right?

07:50.980 --> 07:52.200
Thank you.

07:52.830 --> 07:57.800
When you were kidnapped, 
we confiscated everything in the clinic.

07:58.110 --> 07:59.800
This was part of it.

07:59.800 --> 08:00.710
I see.

08:01.510 --> 08:04.370
<i>The clinic was temporarily closed.</i>

08:04.700 --> 08:08.220
<i>Shenlü, the worker who assisted 
in the escape from the rear palace,</i>

08:08.220 --> 08:14.900
<i>attempted suicide, survived, and was 
imprisoned for her serious crimes.</i>

08:22.030 --> 08:23.320
This is the one.

08:25.310 --> 08:27.530
Are those all drawings of grasshoppers?

08:27.530 --> 08:29.720
Yes, they are.

08:29.720 --> 08:31.720
According to the descriptions 
in the pictures,

08:31.720 --> 08:35.490
they can be separated into two 
major types, or three minor ones.

08:35.900 --> 08:39.140
These are normal grasshoppers.

08:39.140 --> 08:40.710
The illustration shows them in parts,

08:40.710 --> 08:43.340
but it appears this one has shorter wings.

08:43.820 --> 08:47.780
And this is the type we're expecting 
to see more of this year.

08:47.780 --> 08:50.740
It seems like this is the type 
that causes a locust plague.

08:51.650 --> 08:55.350
Hmm. The color's brown instead of green.

08:55.990 --> 08:57.680
These have longer wings, too.

08:59.030 --> 09:04.150
And this is the type that caused 
the small locust plague last year.

09:04.570 --> 09:09.150
So, they change into these brown 
grasshoppers in steps, over time.

09:09.620 --> 09:11.070
That seems to be the case.

09:13.070 --> 09:18.080
<i>Grasshoppers change their body color and 
shape when certain conditions are met.</i>

09:18.410 --> 09:22.480
<i>The changes take several generations, 
and their numbers increase as they change.</i>

09:22.960 --> 09:25.500
<i>Does the multiplication 
cause the shape change,</i>

09:25.500 --> 09:28.160
<i>or does the shape change 
cause the multiplication?</i>

09:28.560 --> 09:32.590
<i>According to the book, 
the former is more likely the cause.</i>

09:32.890 --> 09:39.040
In other words, a small locust plague 
is the precursor to a larger one.

09:40.170 --> 09:44.350
So, we should expect 
a larger locust plague this year.

09:44.950 --> 09:48.320
Yes. I don't know exactly how large.

09:48.790 --> 09:52.320
Does it describe anywhere 
how to prevent this?

09:55.320 --> 09:57.070
No.

09:57.070 --> 10:01.650
It says, once damages are observed, 
we need to eliminate the larvae,

10:01.650 --> 10:03.700
but the only way is lots of manpower.

10:03.700 --> 10:08.190
It also says if they grow to maturity, 
we should light bonfires, but...

10:08.630 --> 10:10.920
That's just the classic way.

10:11.520 --> 10:15.220
There's also a recipe for an insecticide.

10:17.390 --> 10:21.480
I'm sorry. There wasn't 
much of use in here.

10:21.480 --> 10:25.400
No, the insecticide information 
is worth something.

10:26.110 --> 10:28.360
Let's gather the ingredients now.

10:29.920 --> 10:34.240
This is the map of the area 
where locust plagues are occurring.

10:35.250 --> 10:37.030
Do you notice anything?

10:37.480 --> 10:39.330
Notice? Hmm...

10:40.070 --> 10:44.330
Is there more damage in the plains because
 grasshoppers thrive more easily there?

10:44.330 --> 10:51.760
Probably. But this region hasn't seen 
a serious locust plague in decades.

10:53.990 --> 10:55.340
The forest...

10:55.620 --> 10:59.350
I would think, if a forest were near, 
birds would eat the grasshoppers.

10:59.860 --> 11:03.970
The Shihoku-shu region 
was known for its rich forests,

11:03.970 --> 11:06.980
but this area is mostly bare now.

11:07.910 --> 11:11.440
In the late emperor's era, 
strict limits were put on logging.

11:12.010 --> 11:16.200
After he passed away, the Shi clan 
began ignoring those limits.

11:16.950 --> 11:22.080
<i>The late emperor's era... 
The Empress must have banned it.</i>

11:22.400 --> 11:25.440
Perhaps there are more insects 
because there are less birds,

11:25.440 --> 11:26.920
because the trees were cut down?

11:27.570 --> 11:29.640
That's very possible.

11:30.420 --> 11:34.130
I had high hopes for the forest 
resources of Shihoku-shu...

11:34.700 --> 11:35.980
<i>I see.</i>

11:35.980 --> 11:38.140
<i>He was trying to make up 
for the grain shortages</i>

11:38.140 --> 11:41.470
<i>by selling off wood and buying food.</i>

11:41.840 --> 11:46.150
We might run out of ingredients 
for the one insecticide in the book.

11:46.150 --> 11:48.480
I'll prepare other recipes 
as well, just in case.

11:48.880 --> 11:50.270
Yes, please do.

11:50.840 --> 11:55.930
Can we perhaps burn off the areas 
where larvae were spotted?

11:55.930 --> 11:57.460
Depends on the area.

11:57.880 --> 12:01.990
Also... banning hunting 
sparrows would help a little.

12:02.240 --> 12:04.570
Sparrows are a common food source.

12:05.000 --> 12:07.660
If we ban it too suddenly, 
we would get pushback.

12:07.660 --> 12:09.100
If there was something to replace it...

12:09.100 --> 12:09.620
Oh,

12:10.110 --> 12:15.010
why don't we develop a grasshopper 
recipe and call it royal cuisine?

12:17.150 --> 12:21.100
More people would hunt for them 
to deliver to the palace,

12:21.100 --> 12:23.680
and it would spread from 
the palace to the public, too...

12:25.240 --> 12:28.980
<i>This guy... Should I feed him 
the leftover broiled grasshopper?</i>

12:31.560 --> 12:34.660
Can we keep that as a last resort?

12:34.660 --> 12:37.610
Well, we wouldn't have a problem 
if we don't see too many of them.

12:39.310 --> 12:40.320
You're right.

12:41.190 --> 12:43.640
<i>He seems a little more optimistic now.</i>

12:43.640 --> 12:46.920
<i>But are they really that bad to eat?</i>

12:49.500 --> 12:51.040
Um, Master Jinshi.

12:51.330 --> 12:52.580
W-What?

12:53.010 --> 12:57.090
Would you like to have a meal 
with us before you leave?

13:11.600 --> 13:13.900
Please enjoy, Master Jinshi.

13:24.740 --> 13:27.310
Say "ah."

13:28.630 --> 13:30.210
<i>I guess that's enough.</i>

13:36.190 --> 13:41.610
<i>I was going to let him off the hook if he 
was even a bit bothered, but this guy...</i>

13:44.390 --> 13:45.430
Porridge.

13:45.840 --> 13:46.660
Yes.

13:50.320 --> 13:51.350
Please.

13:53.340 --> 13:54.860
<i>Why won't he take it?</i>

13:55.710 --> 13:57.980
<i>Does he not like what's in it?</i>

14:24.900 --> 14:27.470
<i>Perhaps it was a bit 
too shocking for children...</i>

14:29.170 --> 14:31.680
Freckles, I'm taking Zulin away.

14:32.340 --> 14:35.690
Also, man, you need to take 
responsibility for your actions.

14:39.290 --> 14:41.100
<i>I guess that was my bad.</i>

14:51.410 --> 14:52.260
Here.

14:53.760 --> 14:56.000
<i>What is he, a baby?</i>

15:03.820 --> 15:05.750
Hey, Freckles.

15:07.070 --> 15:08.440
Where'd you get that paper?

15:08.440 --> 15:11.060
Oh, Grams gave it to me.

15:11.060 --> 15:13.430
That penny-pincher gave you 
something for free?

15:13.770 --> 15:15.890
What's she up to now?

15:16.220 --> 15:18.340
Anyway, sit down.

15:18.340 --> 15:19.400
Why?

15:19.400 --> 15:22.230
Maomao! Listen to what Chou-u has to say.

15:22.580 --> 15:24.490
And you'll be sleeping here tonight.

15:24.490 --> 15:27.210
We already made a bed 
for you in that other room.

15:27.210 --> 15:28.860
What's wrong, Grams?

15:28.860 --> 15:31.860
Did that weird show I put on 
earlier make you go crazy?

15:31.860 --> 15:32.580
Ow!

15:32.580 --> 15:34.450
Just shut up and do as I say!

15:35.080 --> 15:36.960
<i>So suspicious...</i>

15:47.010 --> 15:48.810
<i>So very suspicious...</i>

15:49.600 --> 15:52.340
Freckles, describe 
the type of guy you like.

15:52.340 --> 15:55.060
Like, "tall," "muscular," stuff like that.

15:55.510 --> 15:56.940
<i>What a bother.</i>

15:57.350 --> 15:58.140
Hmm?

15:59.700 --> 16:01.730
I like 'em not too big.

16:02.140 --> 16:03.610
Hmm.

16:04.160 --> 16:06.950
Plump is better than skinny.

16:06.950 --> 16:08.130
Beard?

16:08.130 --> 16:09.540
I'm not against it.

16:09.540 --> 16:10.820
Face shape?

16:11.190 --> 16:13.910
Soft is better than sharp.

16:14.510 --> 16:16.640
<i>Fox-like eyes would be the worst.</i>

16:16.640 --> 16:18.640
Maomao!

16:18.640 --> 16:19.710
<i>Destroy.</i>

16:19.710 --> 16:22.240
Descending eyebrows, maybe?

16:22.240 --> 16:23.380
Yeah, up to you.

16:23.900 --> 16:25.210
Hmm.

16:25.880 --> 16:27.440
I guess this is it then.

16:29.930 --> 16:32.420
Oh, seems kind of drab.

16:32.420 --> 16:34.710
Looks naive to me.

16:34.710 --> 16:36.510
Yikes, that's a no from me.

16:37.820 --> 16:39.320
What's wrong?

16:39.320 --> 16:42.030
Oh, it looks like someone I know.

16:42.030 --> 16:43.190
What was he like?

16:43.700 --> 16:45.810
He looks just like the rear palace doctor.

16:47.190 --> 16:49.100
Boring.

16:49.100 --> 16:50.880
Come on, let's go.

16:50.880 --> 16:52.820
Time for a bath.

17:09.640 --> 17:12.890
I do understand your feelings, somewhat.

17:13.340 --> 17:14.690
Joka.

17:16.010 --> 17:19.930
Men are fickle things, 
you never know when they change.

17:20.860 --> 17:24.260
That's especially true for men in power.

17:28.990 --> 17:32.530
If you had Pairin's personality, 
I wouldn't stop you.

17:32.530 --> 17:34.660
She's a natural enchantress.

17:35.390 --> 17:38.540
But Maomao, you're different.

17:38.540 --> 17:41.540
If I had to make a comparison,
 you're closer to me.

17:43.750 --> 17:46.700
Every man has changes of heart.

17:46.700 --> 17:49.750
Working here, that's so painfully obvious.

17:49.750 --> 17:51.880
What's the point in believing?

17:57.510 --> 18:01.430
After all, I'm a harlot, 
and you're the daughter of one.

18:03.870 --> 18:05.560
Aren't you smoking a bit too much?

18:05.850 --> 18:07.610
It's fine, I rarely do this.

18:07.610 --> 18:12.570
Those straight-edge bureaucrats 
hate seeing women smoke pipes.

18:21.790 --> 18:24.790
I heard from a customer yesterday 
that there's a sorceress-like girl

18:25.130 --> 18:30.090
who's rarer than the Three 
Princesses of the Verdigris House.

18:30.520 --> 18:34.720
Those high-ranking officials 
sure love oddities.

18:34.720 --> 18:38.260
Yeah yeah, we're too old 
to be of any value.

18:38.620 --> 18:42.040
To think they used to 
treat us like gemstones!

18:42.040 --> 18:43.280
Yeah, yeah.

18:43.860 --> 18:46.730
Wrong. That stone will die there.

18:53.480 --> 18:57.760
<i>Seeing them like this, I feel they're 
still at the top of their game.</i>

18:57.760 --> 19:01.910
According to the stories, 
the sorceress has pure white hair.

19:01.910 --> 19:03.330
And red eyes, too.

19:03.710 --> 19:05.460
<i>That's quite rare.</i>

19:05.460 --> 19:07.420
Oh, an albino then.

19:07.820 --> 19:09.380
Probably.

19:14.580 --> 19:18.640
Very rarely, a person can be 
born without color.

19:18.970 --> 19:21.130
Their eyes are red too, 
because you can see the blood.

19:21.130 --> 19:23.100
They're called albinos, and—

19:23.660 --> 19:26.960
Their hair and skin are very white, 
but they were born that way.

19:26.960 --> 19:29.100
They're the same as us on the inside.

19:29.100 --> 19:31.150
<i>That's what my dad taught me.</i>

19:31.830 --> 19:33.810
A white sorceress, huh?

19:33.810 --> 19:37.700
And they say she uses actual sorcery.

19:39.420 --> 19:42.060
She used to perform in a show tent,

19:42.060 --> 19:45.000
but now you can see her 
at the theater in the city.

19:45.630 --> 19:46.710
<i>Oh, I remember.</i>

19:47.150 --> 19:50.940
<i>Grams was complaining that sales at 
the Verdigris House fell over 20 percent.</i>

19:50.940 --> 19:53.800
<i>I guess people are leaving the pleasure 
district to go to the theater.</i>

19:54.700 --> 19:57.850
Who sees the same show more than once?

19:57.850 --> 19:59.430
You'd be surprised.

20:01.600 --> 20:03.440
Oh, thanks.

20:07.300 --> 20:09.150
Ever heard of liandan-shu?

20:09.460 --> 20:10.900
What brings that up?

20:11.670 --> 20:15.080
<i>The art claiming to create immortal 
sorcerers through medicine.</i>

20:15.080 --> 20:19.530
<i>Dad told me never to try to imitate it, 
as it was completely shady.</i>

20:19.530 --> 20:23.520
They say, in addition to her 
rare appearance,

20:23.520 --> 20:26.450
the sorceress can read 
people's minds and create gold.

20:26.890 --> 20:27.790
Huh.

20:28.190 --> 20:30.460
If you were a high-ranking 
official with doubts,

20:30.460 --> 20:33.130
but had your mind read 
on the spot, how would you feel?

20:33.130 --> 20:34.750
I see.

20:35.180 --> 20:37.210
<i>If you entered doubtful 
and laughing at her,</i>

20:37.210 --> 20:40.840
<i>the feeling gets flipped 
upside down to worship.</i>

20:41.300 --> 20:46.600
<i>That makes it easier to swallow 
the immortality hoax, too.</i>

20:46.890 --> 20:49.500
<i>What a giant pile of idiocy.</i>

20:49.500 --> 20:55.190
So, this so-called sorceress is gathering 
a crowd using claims of immortality?

20:55.510 --> 20:57.460
I don't know that much.

20:57.460 --> 21:01.070
I just overheard the story 
from a follower of an official.

21:01.690 --> 21:06.370
<i>And to think Master Jinshi is racking 
his brains over the locust plague...</i>

21:06.370 --> 21:09.470
<i>The other officials have 
way too much time on their hands.</i>

21:10.580 --> 21:13.850
If you're curious, you could just 
go check her out yourself.

21:13.850 --> 21:16.550
I can't afford the expensive show.

21:16.550 --> 21:19.220
You could just ask.

21:19.840 --> 21:23.980
<i>Ask who? Who has the time for that?</i>

23:45.070 --> 24:00.000
Next Time

23:53.540 --> 23:56.080
<i>Next time: 
